From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core: the TF_GLM_OVN knob registry

ai-engine c60ce5fd1. One registry for the speed-hunt knobs: each is read from the environment
once per process, cached in its own type so every knob has its own statics, and defaults off.
Nothing else reads a knob directly, so a patch that adds a knob adds one entry here.

Gate: applies on the pin; check-native-cuda-host green; whole-tree fmt green; lean
base-vs-head 0 new. This patch is infrastructure and has no speed claim of its own.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0002: the registry's cache key, so each knob gets its own statics
- 0024: `ovn.fake`, the test-only override every knob test drives

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV (a0ffd7ef7 era) make the pin-era getenv(S.key) a new finding: ovn.zig now reads each knob through its .glm row of platform/environment.zig (raw text by profile.lookup, parsed by environment.parse), and a knob with no row is a compile error (environment.registered).
- on() keeps its bool (0 or 1 by the row; GLM's open refuses other text before any read), int() and the new real() and text() return error.BadOvnKnob for text the row refuses; fake() keeps the test-only override.
- cuda_env_test.zig counts GLM's own readers without the TF_GLM_OVN_ rows and checks every knob row instead.
- Cache(key) names its key (`const name = key`) and set() takes `raw`: the first compile (scripts/gates.sh, 2026-11-12) refused an unused parameter and a parameter shadowing ovn.text().
- source: work/fold/0005-ovn-knob-registry.patch

